$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure B for the synthesis of substrate (1): 2–5 To a Schlenk
tube (25-mL) were added Pd(PPh3)4 (114 mg, 0.1 mmol, 5 mol %), CsF (620
mg, 4 mmol, 2.0 equiv), CuI (38 mg, 0.2 mmol, 10 mol %) and substrate 3
(2 mmol). The mixture was closed by a septum, purged by nitrogen gas for
several times then the dry 1,4-dioxane (8 mL) was injected into the
mixture by a syringe and the mixture was allowed to stir for 10 min;
o-bromoiodoarene 4 (2.4 mmol, 1.2 equiv) was then slowly injected into
the mixture by a syringe. The septum was removed and the Schlenk tube was
sealed with cap; again quickly purged by nitrogen gas for several times
and move to oil bath and allowed to stir at 60 °C for 5 h. The crude
reaction mixture was diluted with 30 mL CH2Cl2, filtered through a thin
Celite pad to remove salt and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
isolated through flash column chromatography by using hexane and ethyl
acetate as eluent. Compounds 1. Compounds 1p, 1q, 1G and 1K were obtained
according to this procedure. 3-(2-Bromophenyl)picolinonitrile (1p):
According to the general procedure B, Pd(PPh3)4 (114 mg, 0.1 mmol, 5 mol
%), CsF (620 mg, 4 mmol, 2.0 equiv), CuI (38 mg, 0.2 mmol, 10 mol %),
3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)picolinonitrile (0.46 g, 2
mmol, 1.0 equiv) and o-bromoiodobenzene (0.68 g, 2.4 mmol, 1.2 equiv)
were stirred in dry 1,4-dioxane (8 mL) at 60 °C for 5 h. Work-up and
purification by column chromatography (Hex/EtOAc = 93:7). Product 1p as a
white solid (383 mg, 74%). New compound. mp: 96–97; IR (KBr): 2993, 2240,
1771, 1755, 1377, 1241, 1050 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.74 (d, J
= 4.2 Hz, 1H), 7.81 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.74 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.2 Hz,
1H), 7.59 (dd, .J = 7.8, 4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.46 (td, J = 8.4, 1.2 Hz, 1H),
7.37–7.34 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ 150.0, 141.5, 138.5,
136.2, 133.5, 133.3, 131.0, 130.9. 127.8, 126.0, 122.8, 116.1; HRMS:
C12H7BrN2 calculated 257.9793, found 257.9790.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, slow addition of arene stage 2, sealed tube used
(Schlenk), Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
