$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method A (Reflux Conditions) A mixture of
4-(4-bromo-1-(2-(4-methyl-1H-1,2,3-triazol-1-yl)ethyl)-1H-imidazol-5-
yl)benzonitrile (18) (50 mg, 0.140 mmol),
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan- 2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (58
mg, 0.280 mmol), PdCl2(dppf) (10 mg, 0.014 mmol), BnEt3NCl (3 mg, 0.013
mmol), CsF (65 mg, 0.43 mmol), toluene (2 mL) and water (2 mL) was
stirred at reflux for 42 h.
1-Methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (58
mg, 0.28 mmol), PdCl2(dppf) (10 mg, 0.014 mmol), BnEt3NCl (3 mg, 0.013
mmol) and CsF (65 mg, 0.43 mmol) were added and the mixture was stirred
for a further 3 days. PdCl2(dppf) (20 mg, 0.028 mmol) was added and the
mixture stirred for a further 4 days. The crude material was purified by
Isolute Flash SCX-2 column (100% MeOH to 2 M NH3 in MeOH) followed by
flash column chromatography (0-20% MeOH in CH2Cl2). 7 as a light brown
oil (2.8 mg, 0.0078 mmol, 6%, ≥90% purity). Rf = 0.7 (15% MeOH in
CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (500 MHz, MeOD) δ 7.86 (2H, dat, J = 1.5, 1.5, 8.5 Hz, 2
x ArH), 7.61 (1H, s, ArH), 7.45 (2H, dat, J = 1.5, 1.5, 8.5 Hz, 2 x ArH),
7.43 (1H, br s, ArH), 7.41 (1H, d, J = 0.5 Hz, ArH), 7.25 (1H, d, J = 0.5
Hz, ArH), 4.45-4.51 (4H, m, 2 x CH2), 3.80 (3H, s, CH3), 2.23 (3H, d, J =
0.5 Hz, CH3) ppm; 13C NMR (126 MHz, MeOD) δ 144.6, 139.5, 137.8, 135.4, 2
x 134.1, 132.8, 2 x 129.4, 126.9, 123.9, 119.3, 117.0, 113.9, 51.3, 46.3,
10.3 ppm; IR (oil) 2922, 2852, 1743, 842 cm-1; LCMS (Fast4min) tr = 1.61
min, m/z 359 [M + H]+; purity (AUC) = 95%; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C19H18N8Na [M + Na]+ 381.1547, found [M + Na]+ 381.1557.
